{"case_id":"C002","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration coverage","format-version protocol","encoder/decoder roundtrip semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["meshopt_encodeVertexVersion","meshopt_encodeVertexBufferLevel","meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer"],"reason":"S1 makes vertex format version 1 the valid production configuration, but H0 never selects it. H0 calls meshopt_encodeVertexVersion(0xe) when level < 4 and version 0 otherwise. In S1, 0xe violates assert(unsigned(version) <= 1); without assertions it produces a header that meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer rejects because version > 1. Consequently, H0 does not exercise successful version-1 encoding or encoder-generated version-1 roundtrips, although arbitrary decoder input can incidentally carry a version-1 header.","evidence":["H0 selects meshopt_encodeVertexVersion(level < 4 ? 0xe : 0), so its only selected values are 0xe and 0.","S1 changes meshopt_encodeVertexVersion to assert(unsigned(version) <= 1), establishing 0 and 1 as the valid configurations.","S1 changes meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer to reject version > 1.","S1 production callers select meshopt_encodeVertexVersion(1), including demo/main.cpp, gltf/gltfpack.cpp, tools/codecbench.cpp, and tools/codectest.cpp.","H0's fuzzRoundtrip calls meshopt_encodeVertexBufferLevel and then meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer under the selected version, but never under version 1."],"recommended_action":"Change H0 to select valid versions 0 and 1, and fuzz the level independently so every chosen stride exercises meshopt_encodeVertexBufferLevel followed by meshopt_decodeVertexBuffer for both versions. Retain direct malformed-input decoder fuzzing, including version-1 headers and rejected versions above 1."}
